<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Segovia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Segovia is a city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on a ridge north of the Guadarrama mountains, and capital of the province of the same name. Originally a Celtiberian settlement, it grew under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, whose great aqueduct, probably built around the end of the 1st century CE, still crosses the city. The old town and aqueduct are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/segovia.jpg" alt="Segovia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlos Delgado · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Segovia_-_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
